winewayland: NEUTRON_PEN_GEOM=1 — dump every term of the pen's screen mapping

The trace that root-caused the pen drag-targeting offset. Per pen sample it
prints the hwnd, the surface-local coords, the surface scale, the driver's
surface rect, win32u's authoritative window rect, and the computed screen
point — so the coordinate SPACE of each term is visible instead of inferred.

It killed three of my theories in one run and produced the answer:

  * the pen arithmetic is EXACT — 0 of 2499 samples deviate from
    screen == round(surf*scale) + left;
  * the driver's surface rect and win32u's window rect agree EXACTLY, so
    neither is stale;
  * but the computed position JUMPED (-491,-125) as the pen crossed from
    Premiere's main window into a panel, with 4 ms between samples.

Solving for continuity puts the panel's true origin at (2398.5,1204.9) where
Wine's rect says (1907,1080) — the compositor had moved that popup and Wine
never learned. See xdg_popup_handle_configure(): it stores the compositor's
placement in surface->pending.x/y, which nothing in the driver ever reads.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_tablet.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_tablet.c
@@ -238,6 +238,34 @@
          * on the old behaviour deliberately so that test stayed clean, and then not revisited.
          * Shared helper now -- see wayland_clamp_rounding_overshoot() in wayland_pointer.c. */
         wayland_clamp_rounding_overshoot(&screen, window_rect);
+        /* NEUTRON PEN GEOM (NEUTRON_PEN_GEOM=1): which coordinate SPACE is each term in?
+         * The pen is physically on the Cintiq, which win32u places at x=3840..5760 -- yet a
+         * 2026-08-25 capture had every computed pen position at x=0..3205, i.e. inside the OTHER
+         * monitor's range, while the cursor still tracked the pen correctly on screen. Faithful
+         * injection (cursor == injected, 686/688) does NOT mean the position is right; it means
+         * we are asking for exactly the wrong place. Dump every input to the sum so the space
+         * mismatch is visible instead of inferred. */
+        {
+            const char *pg = getenv("NEUTRON_PEN_GEOM");
+            if (pg && pg[0] == '1')
+            {
+                /* Compare the DRIVER's surface rect against win32u's authoritative window rect
+                 * for the same hwnd. A 2026-08-25 capture showed the computed pen position
+                 * JUMPING 546 px sideways as the pen crossed from Premiere's main window into a
+                 * panel, with no matching physical motion -- and the pen arithmetic itself exact
+                 * on all 2499 samples (screen == round(surf*scale)+left). So one of the two
+                 * window rects disagrees with the other; this says which. */
+                RECT wr = {0};
+                NtUserGetWindowRect(hwnd, &wr, NtUserGetWinMonitorDpi(hwnd, MDT_RAW_DPI));
+                ERR("neutron-pengeom: hwnd=%p surf=(%.3f,%.3f) scale=%.4f "
+                    "surf_rect=(%d,%d)-(%d,%d) win32u_rect=(%d,%d)-(%d,%d) -> screen=(%d,%d)\n",
+                    hwnd, wl_fixed_to_double(x), wl_fixed_to_double(y), surface->window.scale,
+                    (int)window_rect->left, (int)window_rect->top,
+                    (int)window_rect->right, (int)window_rect->bottom,
+                    (int)wr.left, (int)wr.top, (int)wr.right, (int)wr.bottom,
+                    (int)screen.x, (int)screen.y);
+            }
+        }
         wayland_win_data_release(window_data);
         /* NEUTRON: record; the mouse MOVE is injected in wayland_wintab_frame after
          * the packet, so per-sample mouse+packet stay paired and ordered. */
